      en: "St. Joseph Church on Praslin Island was built in the 1930s and serves as a Roman Catholic parish church near Anse Volbert. Constructed from concrete and wood, it features a tall bell tower and a serene interior. Dedicated to Saint Joseph, the patron saint of workers, the church is a focal point for the local community, hosting regular masses and religious events. Praslin, known for its stunning beaches and the UNESCO-listed Vallée de Mai, offers this church as a cultural landmark. The church's architecture blends simplicity with tropical adaptation, providing a peaceful retreat for worshippers and visitors alike.",
